Are you asking about the types of Permanent Establishments (PE)?

A PE is a form of business used by an individual who does not reside in Indonesia, an individual who is present in Indonesia for not more than 183 days within a 12-month period, and an entity that is not established and not domiciled in Indonesia to conduct business or carry out activities in Indonesia, which may take the form of:

a. a place of management;
b. a branch of the company;
c. a representative office;
d. an office building;
e. a factory;
f. a workshop;
g. a warehouse;
h. a space for promotion and sales;
i. mining and extraction of natural resources;
j. an oil and natural gas mining working area;
k. fisheries, animal husbandry, agriculture, plantations, or forestry;
l. a construction, installation, or assembly project;
m. the provision of services in any form by employees or other persons, provided it is performed for more than 60 days within a 12-month period;
n. a person or entity acting as a dependent agent;
o. an agent or employee of an insurance company that is not established and not domiciled in Indonesia, who receives insurance premiums or insures risks in Indonesia; and
p. computers, electronic agents, or automated equipment owned, leased, or used by electronic transaction providers to conduct business activities over the internet.

For regulations regarding the determination of a PE, you can read them by clicking the following link:
